course: dictionary
lesson: 1920
title: Formal words for food
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words sound posh or formal, and writers use them to make a character sound grand, or a little silly. The words around a hard word are its context, and they give clues. «He made one cake, which was two feet across and three feet thick, from flour, water, currants, plums and sugar; Kipling calls it "a Superior Comestible".» A cake is something you eat, so comestible must mean something to eat.
explain: The bracket in the sentence gives you a direct clue: "comestible" means something to eat. When a writer explains a word for you like this, read the bracket carefully and trust it. Then check: does your meaning fit in the sentence?
explain: Comestible can also be an adjective, meaning fit to be eaten. In «comestible plants», the word describes the plants: they are safe and good to eat. An adjective tells you more about a noun, so look for the thing it is describing.
fact: Comestible means something that can be eaten, or food.
fact: As an adjective, comestible means fit to be eaten, or edible.
fact: «Comestibles» is usually plural, as in «the shop sold comestibles».
fact: Comestible is a very formal word, so it can sound funny or posh in a story.
fact: In your own writing, say «food» or «edible» instead of comestible.
exercise: «He made one cake, which was two feet across, from flour, water, currants and sugar.» What does comestible mean in the bracket? | A kind of cloth | Something to wear | *Something to eat | A large metal tin
exercise: A writer says «comestible plants». What kind of word is comestible here? | *An adjective, describing the plants | An adverb, describing how | A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a thing
exercise: Jayden says a comestible is a posh word for a toy. What is the correct meaning? | A wooden box with a lid | A type of musical instrument | A toy for a dog | *Food, or something fit to be eaten
test: The shop had comestibles on sale near the door. What are comestibles? | Clothes and shoes | Toys for the park | Tools for the garden | *Food and things to eat
test: Which word means the same as comestible and is simpler to use in your writing? | curt | glum | *edible | ancient
exam: Why might a writer choose comestible instead of food? | *To sound formal, grand or a little funny | To show that the cake was very small | Because it is the most common word for food | Because it is a spelling mistake
